 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "For each series of premises, draw a logical conclusion to the argument that includes one of the following quantifiers: all, some, or none.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 496174,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<span data-math=\"1 + 2 = 3\">1 + 2 = 3</span>, <span data-math=\"5 + 6 = 11\">5 + 6 = 11</span>, and <span data-math=\"14 + 15 = 29\">14 + 15 = 29</span>. Of these, 1 and 2 are consecutive integers, 5 and 6 are consecutive integers, and 14 and 15 are consecutive integers. Also, their sums, 3, 11, and 29 are all prime numbers. Prime numbers are positive integers greater than one that are only divisible by one and the number itself. What conclusion can you draw from these premises?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "It would be incorrect to say that the sum of all consecutive integers results in a prime number because 0 and <span data-math=\"1 = 1\"></span>, which is not prime. You can say that “The sum of some consecutive integers results in a prime number.”"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "The sum of some consecutive integers results in a prime number."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 496175,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "A robin is a bird that lays blue eggs. A chicken is a bird that typically  lays white and brown eggs. An ostrich is a bird that lays exceptionally large eggs. If a bird lays eggs, then they do not give live birth to their young. What conclusion can you draw from these premises?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "Based on the premises provided, no birds give live birth to their young. This statement, however, is false, as some birds do give birth to live young."
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<p>No birds give live birth to their young.</p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 496176,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "All parallelograms have four sides. All rectangles are parallelograms. All squares are rectangles. What additional conclusion can you make about squares from these premises?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>All squares are rectangles. All rectangles are parallelograms, so a square is a parallelogram. All parallelograms have four sides, so a square has four sides. Thus, all squares have four sides.</p>\n<p>You could draw a Venn diagram that shows this. Squares are a subset of rectangles. Rectangles are a subset of parallelograms. Parallelograms are a subset of things with four sides. Thus, squares are a subset of things with four sides.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<p>All squares are parallelograms and have four sides.</p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
